# zig-only
# A leader chord resolves on its second key, however fast it is typed:
# `space e` toggles the sidebar and `space f f` opens the file picker
# with no wait between the keys (Neovim resolves the mapping on the key,
# not on `timeoutlen`). The `e` must not run as the end-of-word motion —
# the cursor stays on column 1 — and Esc on a pending leader cancels it
# without opening which-key. The runner settles and expires chords after
# every `key` step, so the fast typing is a `type` step — its keys go in
# back to back.
write b.zig "const std = @import(\"std\");\n"
open b.zig
command editor.use_vim
expect screen contains "● mnml-e2e-"
expect screen contains "Col 1 "
type " e"
expect screen lacks "● mnml-e2e-"
expect screen contains "Col 1 "
expect screen lacks "╭ Leader"
type " e"
expect screen contains "● mnml-e2e-"
expect screen contains "Col 1 "
type " ff"
expect screen contains "╭ Files"
key esc
expect screen lacks "╭ Files"
key space
key esc
wait 700
expect screen lacks "╭ Leader"
expect screen contains "Col 1 "
